        "verdict": "PASS",
        "reasons": "CONDITIONAL is the right stance. Four written acceptances at $900 are recorded on the card: 4 x $900 = $3,600 against $3,000, and no new sales are needed. Brain-produced fulfilment, $10 cost and $0 exposure are evidence. The one unknown is when the money settles, and the plan confirms each co-op's payment terms on day 1-3 before delivering. Stop rules: terms beyond day 30, or a withdrawal. One withdrawal leaves $2,700, under $3,000, which the stop rule correctly catches. Cost of $40 is paid from fees, with no capital needed.",
